  "verbalization": "Tolazamide is linked to Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus through a series of indications that suggest a potential role in the pathophysiology of the disease. The evidence shows that Tolazamide is associated with Diabetes Mellitus, which in turn is linked to two other drugs—Gemigliptin, Teneligliptin, and Trelagliptin—each of which is indicated for Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus. This suggests a possible indirect relationship between Tolazamide and the disease, possibly through its effects on glucose regulation or metabolic pathways. The shared indication for Diabetes Mellitus among the linked drugs implies a common mechanism or target, though the exact nature of this relationship remains unclear. The evidence supports a potential pathway where Tolazamide may influence glucose metabolism, but further research is needed to confirm its direct role in the development or management of Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus.",
